# These files are checked out byte for byte or the fixtures stop being fixtures.
#
# `<slug>.result.json` records a sha256 over `<slug>.txt` and `<slug>.srt`, and a checkout that
# turned their line endings into CRLF would change those bytes and fail
# `test_the_engine_result_document_describes_the_bytes_beside_it` on somebody else's machine and
# nowhere else. `-text` on everything here is what stops git touching them at all.
* -text
